<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammira Deva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1301">1301</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Hammiradeva</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hammira Deva was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> king of Ranthambore in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> from about 1283 to 1301, the last ruler of the Chahamanas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranthambore-fort">Ranastambhapura</a>. He raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> and Mewar, and sheltered Mongol rebels who had fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a>'s army; Alauddin besieged Ranthambore for months and took it in 1301, when Hammira was killed. He became a hero of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> legend through works such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammira-mahakavya">Hammira Mahakavya</a>.</p></div>
